--TEST--
`Core\Response::sendFile` inside a request leaves a name, and `nvs run --request` sends the named file as the body the way a server does —`rule:security/response-body-is-one-typed-member`
--GET--
page=about
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A context answering a request records the name and reads nothing. The
// finish path that a server runs at its connection is what opens the file, so
// a run under `--request` has to run that half too, or the body is empty.
Core\Response::sendFile("page.html");
--FILE page.html--
<h1>About</h1>
<p>tea &amp; cake</p>
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
--EXPECT--
<h1>About</h1>
<p>tea &amp; cake</p>
